Your friend Conan opens the door. Conan is broad-shouldered, pugnacious, and brawny. Nevertheless, he stands by his friends through thick and thin.

Conan's room resembles a military barracks, perhaps influenced by his father's upbringing. A handmade bow hangs on the wall—a gift from his father. A horizontal bar is screwed into the corner.

"So, Henry, are you ready?!"

"Yeah, buddy, of course! Shall we go?"

"You bet! By the way," he lowers his voice. "What about taking my father's rifle? He's out and won't come home until evening."